      "location": "sections/homily/10-body.tex:9\u201313",
      "problem": "The second mention of 'the disciples' can sound like the very disciples who asked Jesus about the Temple would have to flee in Judea. Chrysostom's Homily 76 \u00a71 expressly places the Apostles elsewhere by the time of the siege, and Mt 24:16 gives the warning to those in Judea. The reading of the two events and the prayer Jesus asks for remain clear.",
      "required_result": "Name those in Judea as the people who must heed the warning and flee. Keep the disciples' question and Christ's final gathering in their present roles.",
